{% comment %}
  "Need any help?" - a bordered card on a hatched ground, with the contact
  channels ranged right and the opening hours underneath.

  A section of its own rather than part of pdp-info-columns, and rather than the
  size-help block it replaces in the buy box. Two reasons:

  - It is brand-level, identical on every product, and it belongs at the foot of
    the page rather than between the size chips and the buy buttons.
  - A section can be dragged in from the theme editor. That matters in this
    theme: pushing templates/*.json does not reliably reach the store, so a
    preset is the way to place this even when the template change does not
    take. Every setting carries a default, so a section added by hand renders
    complete without anyone filling a field.

  The channels are blocks, so a store can show a phone number and WhatsApp, or
  add Instagram, an email address and a shop address, without a code change
  each time. Each block says what kind of link it is and the href is built to
  suit: `tel:` keeps the plus sign and drops the spaces, `wa.me` drops the plus
  sign as well because it rejects one, `mailto:` is passed through as typed.

  That is also why the number shown and the number linked are one field here
  and were two before. The old pair existed because a single field could not
  serve both a `tel:` href and a `wa.me` href - `+91 93197 50031` is valid for
  one and rejected by the other. With the block declaring which kind of link it
  is, the stripping is decided per channel and the merchant types the number
  once, in whatever shape reads best.

  Legacy: a section with no blocks at all - which is every template that
  already had this section, since templates/*.json carry its settings and no
  blocks - falls back to the old Call and WhatsApp settings. So this deploys
  without touching a template, and a merchant who then adds a channel block
  takes over from the fallback completely.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'product-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  comment
    The channels, flattened into four lists read by one loop below. Liquid
    cannot build an array of objects, and the alternative - a block loop plus a
    second, near-identical legacy branch in the markup - is two copies of the
    row markup that drift apart the first time one is styled.

    A blank entry would leave two delimiters together and shift every channel
    after it onto the wrong row, so every list carries a value for every
    surviving channel: '-' for "no link", '0'/'1' for the flags.
  endcomment
  assign ch_icons = ''
  assign ch_labels = ''
  assign ch_hrefs = ''
  assign ch_external = ''
  assign ch_count = 0

  for block in section.blocks
    unless block.type == 'channel'
      continue
    endunless

    assign label = block.settings.label | strip
    comment
      The label is what the shopper clicks, so a channel without one has
      nothing to show even if its number is filled in.
    endcomment
    if label == blank
      continue
    endif

    assign value = block.settings.value | strip
    assign href = '-'
    assign external = '0'

    case block.settings.action
      when 'call'
        comment
          `tel:` accepts the plus sign and the country code, and wants the
          spaces and dashes gone.
        endcomment
        assign digits = value | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | strip
        if digits != blank
          assign href = 'tel:' | append: digits
        endif
      when 'whatsapp'
        comment
          wa.me rejects spaces, plus signs and dashes outright - it does not
          redirect, it errors - so all three go.
        endcomment
        assign digits = value | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-' | strip
        if digits != blank
          assign href = 'https://wa.me/' | append: digits
          assign external = '1'
        endif
      when 'email'
        if value != blank
          assign href = 'mailto:' | append: value
        endif
      when 'link'
        if block.settings.url != blank
          assign href = block.settings.url
          assign external = '1'
        endif
    endcase

    comment
      Resolved into a variable first. `ch_icons | append: x | default: 'none'`
      reads as if the default guards x, but it guards the whole accumulated
      string - which is only ever blank on the first channel, so a missing icon
      on the second would append nothing and shift every icon after it.
    endcomment
    assign icon_name = block.settings.icon | default: 'none'
    assign ch_icons = ch_icons | append: icon_name | append: '~|~'
    assign ch_labels = ch_labels | append: label | append: '~|~'
    assign ch_hrefs = ch_hrefs | append: href | append: '~|~'
    assign ch_external = ch_external | append: external | append: '~|~'
    assign ch_count = ch_count | plus: 1
  endfor

  comment
    No blocks means a section placed before the blocks existed. Rebuild the two
    channels it used to hard-code, from the settings it already carries, so an
    existing template renders exactly as it did.
  endcomment
  if ch_count == 0
    if section.settings.call_label != blank
      assign digits = section.settings.call_number | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | strip
      assign href = '-'
      if digits != blank
        assign href = 'tel:' | append: digits
      endif
      assign ch_icons = ch_icons | append: 'phone' | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_labels = ch_labels | append: section.settings.call_label | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_hrefs = ch_hrefs | append: href | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_external = ch_external | append: '0' | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_count = ch_count | plus: 1
    endif

    if section.settings.chat_label != blank
      assign digits = section.settings.chat_number | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-' | strip
      assign href = '-'
      assign external = '0'
      if digits != blank
        assign href = 'https://wa.me/' | append: digits
        assign external = '1'
      endif
      assign ch_icons = ch_icons | append: 'whatsapp' | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_labels = ch_labels | append: section.settings.chat_label | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_hrefs = ch_hrefs | append: href | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_external = ch_external | append: external | append: '~|~'
      assign ch_count = ch_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endif

  assign icon_list = ch_icons | split: '~|~'
  assign label_list = ch_labels | split: '~|~'
  assign href_list = ch_hrefs | split: '~|~'
  assign external_list = ch_external | split: '~|~'

  assign show = false
  if section.settings.title != blank or ch_count > 0
    assign show = true
  endif

  comment
    Two channels fit beside the copy on a phone and the reviewed design keeps
    them there. Three do not - they either wrap into the hours or squeeze the
    title to nothing - so from three up the card stacks on small screens
    instead. The count decides it here rather than CSS guessing at it, because
    `:has()` cannot count children and a wrap-based fix cannot tell a deliberate
    two-line layout from a collapse.
  endcomment
  assign stack = false
  if ch_count > 2
    assign stack = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if show -%}
  <div
    class="pdp-section pdp-needhelp-section color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
    style="--pdp-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --pdp-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px; --pdp-needhelp-width: {{ section.settings.card_width }}px;"
  >
    <div class="pdp-section__inner">
      <div class="pdp-needhelp">
        <div class="pdp-needhelp__card{% if stack %} pdp-needhelp__card--stack{% endif %}">
          {%- comment -%}
            One paragraph, two spans. The card is a single row - copy left,
            actions right - so the two lines run on as one sentence on a desktop
            and break after the first on a phone, where the row is tight enough
            that "Need any help? Get in touch." wrapping mid-phrase looked like
            an accident. The break is CSS on the spans rather than a <br>, so
            there is one piece of markup for both widths and nothing to hide.

            Kept as two settings because that is how the copy is written and
            reviewed, and because the break needs to know where line one ends.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="pdp-needhelp__text">
            <p class="pdp-needhelp__title">
              {%- if section.settings.title != blank -%}
                <span class="pdp-needhelp__line">{{ section.settings.title | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if section.settings.subtitle != blank -%}
                <span class="pdp-needhelp__line">{{ section.settings.subtitle | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </p>
          </div>

          {%- if ch_count > 0 -%}
            <ul class="pdp-needhelp__actions">
              {%- for label in label_list -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign href = href_list[forloop.index0]
                  assign icon_name = icon_list[forloop.index0]
                  assign is_external = false
                  if external_list[forloop.index0] == '1'
                    assign is_external = true
                  endif
                -%}
                <li>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    A channel with a label and no usable number still shows, as
                    text rather than a link. That is deliberate: a phone number
                    written into the label with nothing in the number field is a
                    half-finished setup, and showing it unlinked makes that
                    visible on the page instead of hiding the whole row.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- if href != '-' -%}
                    <a
                      class="pdp-needhelp__action"
                      href="{{ href }}"
                      {% if is_external %}
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener"
                      {% endif %}
                    >
                      {%- if icon_name != 'none' -%}
                        {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: icon_name -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <span>{{ label | escape }}</span>
                    </a>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="pdp-needhelp__action">
                      {%- if icon_name != 'none' -%}
                        {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: icon_name -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <span>{{ label | escape }}</span>
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.hours != blank -%}
            <p class="pdp-needhelp__hours">{{ section.settings.hours | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP: Need any help",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "pdp-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "Line one",
      "default": "Need any help?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subtitle",
      "label": "Line two",
      "default": "Get in touch.",
      "info": "Runs on after line one on a desktop and moves to its own line on a phone."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hours",
      "label": "Hours",
      "default": "Mon-Sat 9:30 AM TO 5:30 PM (IST)"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_width",
      "min": 600,
      "max": 1500,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Maximum width",
      "default": 1000,
      "info": "Caps the card and centres it. Below this width it simply fills the section."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Fallback: Call and WhatsApp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Used only while no Contact blocks have been added. Add a block and these are ignored — so an existing page keeps working untouched, and moving to blocks is one step rather than a migration."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "call_label",
      "label": "Call: link text",
      "default": "Call"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "call_number",
      "label": "Call: number",
      "default": "+919319750031",
      "info": "With the country code. A plus sign is fine here — tel: accepts it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "chat_label",
      "label": "WhatsApp: link text",
      "default": "Chat"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "chat_number",
      "label": "WhatsApp: number",
      "default": "919319750031",
      "info": "Digits only — wa.me rejects spaces and plus signs."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.colors.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.colors.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.padding.section_padding_heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_top",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_bottom",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "channel",
      "name": "Contact",
      "limit": 6,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "One channel — a phone number, WhatsApp, an email address, a social profile or a shop address. Type the number however it reads best; the link is built to suit the action chosen below."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "icon",
          "label": "Icon",
          "default": "phone",
          "options": [
            { "value": "phone", "label": "Phone" },
            { "value": "whatsapp", "label": "WhatsApp" },
            { "value": "chat", "label": "Chat" },
            { "value": "email", "label": "Email" },
            { "value": "instagram", "label": "Instagram" },
            { "value": "facebook", "label": "Facebook" },
            { "value": "youtube", "label": "YouTube" },
            { "value": "pinterest", "label": "Pinterest" },
            { "value": "tiktok", "label": "TikTok" },
            { "value": "twitter", "label": "X / Twitter" },
            { "value": "linkedin", "label": "LinkedIn" },
            { "value": "telegram", "label": "Telegram" },
            { "value": "map-pin", "label": "Address" },
            { "value": "globe", "label": "Website" },
            { "value": "none", "label": "No icon" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Link text",
          "default": "Call",
          "info": "What the shopper reads — a word like Call, or the number itself. Leave empty to hide this channel."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "action",
          "label": "Action",
          "default": "call",
          "info": "Decides how the number below is turned into a link.",
          "options": [
            { "value": "call", "label": "Start a phone call" },
            { "value": "whatsapp", "label": "Open WhatsApp" },
            { "value": "email", "label": "Open an email" },
            { "value": "link", "label": "Open a link" },
            { "value": "none", "label": "Show as text, no link" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "value",
          "label": "Number or email address",
          "default": "+91 93197 50031",
          "info": "For Call, WhatsApp and Email. Include the country code on a number; spaces, dashes and a plus sign are all fine and are stripped where the link needs them gone."
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "url",
          "label": "Link",
          "info": "Used only when the action is Open a link — an Instagram profile, a contact page, a map."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "PDP: Need any help",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "channel",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "phone",
            "label": "Call",
            "action": "call",
            "value": "+91 93197 50031"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "channel",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "whatsapp",
            "label": "Chat",
            "action": "whatsapp",
            "value": "+91 93197 50031"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
